        <div class="block__panel" id="panel-threads" role="region" aria-label="Projects">
          <div class="block__panelInner"><div class="block__content">

            <div class="sub">
              <p class="sub__label">Einstein Telescope</p>
              <p>A planned European observatory of two or three 10-kilometre arms in underground tunnels, using cryogenic mirrors to reach roughly ten times the sensitivity of today's detectors. Sites under study are in Sardinia, the Euregio Meuse-Rhine region, and Lusatia in Saxony.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><a href="https://auger.ifj.edu.pl/eng/et.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">What IFJ PAN contributes</a></li>
                <li><a href="https://einsteintelescope.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Project overview and status</a></li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="sub">
              <p class="sub__label">Related programmes at the Institute</p>
              <ul>
                <li><a href="https://astrophys.ifj.edu.pl/en/cosmic-rays-gamma-ray-astrophysics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cosmic rays and gamma-ray astrophysics</a></li>
                <li><a href="https://astrophys.ifj.edu.pl/en/neutrino-astrophysics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Neutrino astrophysics</a></li>
                <li><a href="https://web.ifj.edu.pl/en/divisions/no1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Division of Particle and Astroparticle Physics</a></li>
                <li><a href="https://web.ifj.edu.pl/en/research/research-projects/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Funded projects at IFJ PAN</a></li>
              </ul>
